  "releaseNotes": "Core Formatting Improvements:\n      - Refactored internal code structure for cleaner, more consistent formatting across all core modules.\n      - Improved readability and maintainability without altering any existing public syntax or APIs.\n      - Standardized method layouts, inline optimizations, and attribute placement for better long‑term extensibility.\n\n      Handler Enhancements:\n      - Added unified fast‑response helpers for `Ok` and `Error` across HTTP, HTTPS, WS, and WSS transports.\n      - Introduced WebSocket‑aware error handling that automatically switches to binary error packets when in WS/WSS mode.\n      - Ensured consistent behavior between secure and non-secure transports while preserving protocol‑specific semantics.\n\n      Object Pooling Improvements:\n      - Added `Empty` static instances for pooled types such as `PacketModel` to support lightweight operations without unnecessary allocations.\n      - Implemented proper `Dispose` support for all classes inheriting from `PooledObject`, ensuring buffers and resources are always returned safely to the pool.\n      - Reduced overhead in common fast‑path scenarios by eliminating redundant rent/return cycles.\n\n      Performance and Stability:\n      - Optimized zero‑copy packet building paths for lower latency under high throughput.\n      - Improved internal batching and ordering mechanisms to ensure consistent delivery even under concurrent load.\n      - Strengthened session‑lifecycle safety to prevent accidental sends on closed or invalid connections.",
